  "finalText": "I merged the three duplicate search reports into T-1052. It is now sev2 and assigned to E-201 Ines Kovac.\n\n- **Merged:** T-1053 and T-1054 are folded into T-1052, the earliest-created report. All three described CRM account search returning a 500 on every query.\n- **Deadline:** T-1052 now carries 2026-03-17T12:40Z, the earliest deadline committed on any of the three (it came from T-1053). It was 15:05Z before. I did not change it again when regrading.\n- **Severity:** sev2. The merge raised the impact scope to department, and the matrix maps CRM plus department to sev2.\n- **Assignee:** E-201 Ines Kovac. She is the business-apps on-call at 12:40Z, when the deadline falls. T-1053's previous assignee, E-202, is not on call at that time, so he did not carry over.\n- **Links:** the merge moved T-1054's link to T-1061 onto T-1052, and T-1061 now points at T-1052. T-1061 is otherwise unchanged and still open.\n- **Left alone:** T-1055 (CSV export returns an empty file) has a different root cause and the requester says search works, so I didn't touch it. T-1061 is the engineering tracking ticket for the index rebuild, not a duplicate report, so I didn't merge or close it.\n- **Not done:** I didn't escalate, since you asked only for grading and assignment. If you want it, sev2 goes to platform-primary.\n- **Comment:** I added a note on T-1052 recording the merge, deadline, severity and assignment. I did not comment on the two merged tickets.",
